# Gate^Flame control app — environment.
#
# Copy to .env.local. Nothing here is a secret: every VITE_ variable is baked
# into the shipped bundle and readable by anyone with the APK or the page
# source. The node device token is NOT a build-time value — it is issued at
# pairing and lives only in the handset. See docs/PAIRING-AND-TELEMETRY.md.
#
# Every variable below is optional. With none of them set, the app discovers a
# node on the LAN and falls back to clearly-labelled simulated data if none
# answers.

# ── Node connection ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pin a specific node instead of discovering one. Handy in development.
# Leave unset in production — the app finds gateflame.local over mDNS, then
# tries the common LAN addresses.
# VITE_NODE_BASE_URL="http://192.168.1.105"

# Request timeout, milliseconds. Default 4000.
# VITE_API_TIMEOUT_MS="4000"

# Telemetry poll interval, milliseconds. Default 4000.
# VITE_POLL_INTERVAL_MS="4000"

# ── Data source ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Force simulated data even when a node is reachable. For sales demos and for
# UI work without hardware. The SIMULATED DATA banner is shown either way —
# it is not suppressible, by design.
# VITE_USE_MOCK_DATA="true"

# Never fall back to simulation. Connection failures surface as errors instead
# of demo data. Use in QA so a broken API cannot hide behind plausible numbers.
# VITE_STRICT_LIVE="true"

# ── Note on GEMINI_API_KEY / APP_URL ──────────────────────────────────
# Earlier versions of this file declared GEMINI_API_KEY and APP_URL. Neither is
# read anywhere in the application: there is no `import.meta.env` reference to
# either, no `define:` block in any Vite config, and `@google/genai` is imported
# by no source file. They were AI Studio scaffolding. They are removed rather
# than left to imply a setup step that does nothing.
#
# If Gemini features are added later, note that a key exposed to the client is
# a key published to every customer. Server-side proxying is the only safe
# shape for it.
